<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea H1 oil products demand lowest in 12 yrs.</title>
<headline>S.Korea H1 oil products demand lowest in 12 yrs.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's oil products demand grew 1.9 percent to 369.4 million barrels in the first half of 1997 from 362.5 million a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>This marked the slowest first-half growth in 12 years.</p>
<p>It compared with a 7.6 percent rise in domestic demand in the same period of last year.</p>
<p>The ministry said demand growth for oil products slowed due to an industrial downturn and high oil product prices.  </p>
<p>The statement said oil refiners produced 424.9 million barrels of petroleum products in the first half against 338.3 million a year before.</p>
<p>South Korea currently has a refining capacity of 2.44 million bpd.  </p>
<p>Oil products demand (in million barrels)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	  H1 1996</p>
<p>    TOTAL			  369.4	    362.5</p>
<p>MAJOR PRODUCTS</p>
<p>     gasoline		     33.1	     33.0</p>
<p>     kerosene		     40.7	     39.3</p>
<p>     diesel			 84.4	     90.6</p>
<p>     C-type fuel oil	    85.0	     82.3</p>
<p>     naphtha			73.7	     66.9</p>
<p>     LPG			    35.8	     35.3</p>
<p>-- Seoul newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
